Yes! I finally ascended Mike the Lady after more than four years of playing
nethack. I didn't cheat - only got 2 wishes from the wand of wishing. One 
from a magic lamp which I used as an ordinary lamp until it started to ficker.
Two djinnis, two magic markers and lots of preparation. The Gnomish mines
are a great proving ground - if you can make it there, you'll make it anywhere
(my kinda town). Found Fort Ludios by chance - first time I'd been able to
dig into a vault. Nearly died laughing at the message you get when you've
robbed a vault:-). 

>  Come to think of it, anyone finish 3.0j without any of the above
>cheating methods (slight or blatant)?

I made it into the endgame once on 3.0j and learnt a valuable lesson about
rings of conflict. Apart from that the furthest I'd been was 1st level of
hell (died in the moat:-().

This time I fell into water no less than _seven_ times - thank you Dev Team
for that get out.

In 3.1 I think that the luckstone biases the game too much in your favour -
find a luckstone, an alter and a (few) wand(s) of create monster and you
will soon maxout your luck. I didn't need to pray until I nearly starved in
one of the maze levels above the castle, my God did so much to help me
(including giving me a blessed rustproof +3 Vorpal Blade) that I never looked
back.

The quest was straight forward, valkyries get lots of giants, but by then I
had cleared Ludios and a Treasure Zoo with four (count'em 4!) Gray Dragons.
Boy was I surprised when those dragon scales poly'ed into a leather armor!
3.1 is different enough to make you think and consistent enough to make
that thought really constructive.

Genocide helped a lot (got two from Vlad's Throne). It's wonderful to watch
a demilich grow up into a Lich and die! Over 100K turns, no auto-pickup
and then the endgame - wow! I had two segmentaion faults - recover worked
like a charm and then ascended with 7.5 Million points. The only part of the
game I feel is still lacking is gems - there ought to be a way to learn
about gems and use them to your advantage.

I picked up every wand of cancellation I found, every wand of death. Getting
into the Sanctum was fun - I've never deliberately polyself'ed before.
Everytime the Wizard appeared, I zapped him with cancel, then Vorpal until
his head fell off. Once I got the Vorpal Blade, I hardly used Mjollnir at
all.

Over 100K turns, no auto-pickup and then the endgame - wow! I had a total of
two segmentaion faults - recover worked like a charm and then ascended with
7.5 Million points. The only part of the game I feel is still lacking is
gems - there ought to be a way to learn about gems and use them to your
advantage.

The News feed to the UK has been a bit erratic of late, so we haven't seen
patch 1 yet.

Thank you Dev Team - another happy customer.

Mike.

